1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,695
…or high-intensity interval training.

2
00:00:01,695 --> 00:00:03,622
I'll give that 7 out of 10.

3
00:00:03,622 --> 00:00:05,422
It's a wonderful mode of exercise,

4
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:06,279
good for the heart,

5
00:00:06,279 --> 00:00:08,289
good for cardiovascular conditioning.

6
00:00:08,289 --> 00:00:09,169
However,

7
00:00:09,169 --> 00:00:10,809
there's a very strong point of concern

8
00:00:10,809 --> 00:00:12,349
for patients who have caught underlying

9
00:00:12,349 --> 00:00:13,989
cardiovascular diseases.

10
00:00:13,989 --> 00:00:15,369
So it has to be done under the supervision

11
00:00:15,369 --> 00:00:16,909
of an expert cardiologist.

12
00:00:16,909 --> 00:00:18,769
Or in order to avoid

13
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:20,009
the higher incidence

14
00:00:20,009 --> 00:00:21,829
of mortality or mobility,

15
00:00:21,829 --> 00:00:23,229
it should be better avoided in patients

16
00:00:23,229 --> 00:00:24,949
who have got cardiovascular diseases.

17
00:00:24,949 --> 00:00:25,869
But for normal patients

18
00:00:25,869 --> 00:00:27,869
to improve endurance and stamina,

19
00:00:27,869 --> 00:00:29,509
it is an excellent form of exercise.

20
00:00:29,509 --> 00:00:31,127
That's why I'm giving that 7 out of 10.
